cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use the FactsPack (.pack) format or this specification, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "FactsPack (.pack): a token-efficient, agent-first wire format for structured data"
abstract: >-
  FactsPack is a line-oriented, UTF-8, tab-separated text format for
  streaming structured tabular data to AI agents at roughly one-fifth the
  token cost of JSON. It combines schema-once positional rows, in-band
  dictionary interning of repeated strings, multi-table streams,
  incremental add/delete rows, hash-linked master/diff chains tuned for
  LLM prompt-cache economics, an in-band plain-language legend for cold
  reading, an integrity trailer for truncation/tamper detection, and
  explicit trust rules (untrusted-data, freshness, determinism).
authors:
